The viable family is now concrete: a native one-dimensional weighted point graph, represented through an affine residue coordinate. A witness is a short list of cut ranks; verification only recomputes its exact integer edit cost. The paper’s Theorem 2 gives the \(O(n^2)\) reference dynamic program (so this is explicitly Track B), while the intended shortcut is to recognize the hidden line coordinate and bucket the points—under 300 arithmetic operations at the planned shipping size. I’m stress-testing that planting against transformed-gap and agglomerative heuristics before committing it to the module.
